        "severity": "minor",
        "evidence": "markov-disambiguation.md:16-20 defines the Markov-chain transition probability p_{w→w'} = tr_M(ρ(w'))·conj(tr_M(ρ(w'))) / Σ tr_M(ρ(w''))·conj(...) — the numerator depends only on w' (the target), not on the source w, so the 'transition' is independent of the originating state w.",
        "notes": "As written the transition kernel p_{w→w'} has no w-dependence, making it a fixed target distribution rather than a genuine Markov transition; likely a typo where one factor should be tr_M(ρ(w)) or a Hecke matrix element ⟨w|·|w'⟩. The reduction 'at real q0 reduces to |tr_M|^2' is consistent with this reading. Minor — disambiguation intent is clear, but the displayed kernel is ill-typed as a transition probability."
      }
